{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "avft",
    "description": "Template library: AVFTControlStrategy, MOVES 5's Alternative Vehicle Fuels & Technologies control strategy (PLAN.md §7.3.78, docs/esm-conventions.md §129). MOVES runs it whenever the execution database's `avft` table has a row (MOVESInstantiator.addAutomaticInternalControlStrategies, java:1718-1806), before any generator: AVFTMasterLoopable.doDatabaseUpdatesUsingAVFTTable joins each avft row to sourceTypeModelYear and runspecModelYear and hands it to applyNewFraction, which compares the row's fuelEngFraction, cast to float, with `old` -- sum(stmyFraction) of sampleVehiclePopulation over regulatory class at the row's (sourceTypeModelYearID, fuelTypeID, engTechID), read before any row is rewritten -- and issues one UPDATE of sampleVehiclePopulation for that combination: ADD when new - old >= 1e-6, SUBTRACT when new - old <= -1e-6, nothing otherwise. A combination sampleVehiclePopulation has no row for is ignored (its `tableFraction.find` misses). Then ExecutionRunSpec.runUpdateScript reruns UpdateExecution.sql, which rebuilds RegClassSourceTypeFraction from the rewritten table.\n\nTHE TWO BRANCHES ARE NOT ONE FORMULA WRITTEN TWICE. ADD sets stmyFraction = stmyFuelEngFraction x new: the regulatory-class split comes from stmyFuelEngFraction, which is defined on a row whose stmyFraction is 0, so ADD is the only branch that can move vehicles INTO a combination the default fleet does not have (a source bin SourceBinDistributionGenerator's `stmyFraction > 0.0` then admits). SUBTRACT scales the rows in place, stmyFraction x new / old, so it keeps whatever split they had. In the national default the two agree wherever old > 0 (stmyFraction / old equals stmyFuelEngFraction there to 1.2e-15), so the asymmetry shows only at old = 0, where SUBTRACT cannot fire. The float cast moves `new` and `old` by at most half a float ulp (3e-8 near 1), which changes the branch only within that distance of the 1e-6 threshold and changes the rewritten fraction by less than the FLOAT column MOVES stores it in already rounds to; it is not reproduced.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "control-strategy",
      "avft",
      "onroad"
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "avft_branch": {
      "description": "applyNewFraction's decision for one sample-vehicle combination: 1 (ADD) when the avft states it and `new_fraction - old_fraction >= 1e-6`, -1 (SUBTRACT) when it states it and the difference is `<= -1e-6`, and 0 otherwise -- a combination the avft does not state (`stated` 0), or one it restates within the threshold. AVFTMasterLoopable.java applyNewFraction.",
      "params": [
        "stated",
        "old_fraction",
        "new_fraction"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": ">",
            "args": [
              "stated",
              0.0
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">=",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "new_fraction",
                      "old_fraction"
                    ]
                  },
                  1e-06
                ]
              },
              1.0,
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "<=",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "-",
                        "args": [
                          "new_fraction",
                          "old_fraction"
                        ]
                      },
                      -1e-06
                    ]
                  },
                  -1.0,
                  0.0
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "avft_rewritten_fraction": {
      "description": "A sample-vehicle row's stmyFraction after AVFTMasterLoopable: under ADD (`branch` 1) `UPDATE sampleVehiclePopulation SET stmyFraction = stmyFuelEngFraction * new`, under SUBTRACT (-1) `SET stmyFraction = stmyFraction * new / old` (old > 0 whenever SUBTRACT fires, since new >= 0; the guard only keeps the untaken branch finite), and otherwise the row as it was. `branch` is `avft_branch`'s.",
      "params": [
        "branch",
        "stmy_fraction",
        "fuel_engine_fraction",
        "old_fraction",
        "new_fraction"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": ">",
            "args": [
              "branch",
              0.5
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "fuel_engine_fraction",
              "new_fraction"
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "<",
                "args": [
                  "branch",
                  -0.5
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": ">",
                    "args": [
                      "old_fraction",
                      0.0
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          "stmy_fraction",
                          "new_fraction"
                        ]
                      },
                      "old_fraction"
                    ]
                  },
                  0.0
                ]
              },
              "stmy_fraction"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
